:name: STM32 secure OTA bootloader
:description: STM32F407 with the bootloader and a factory image in slot A.

# Usage from the Renode monitor (paths relative to the repository root):
#   (monitor) $build=@build/fw
#   (monitor) include @renode/stm32f407.resc
#   (monitor) start
# The console (USART2) is shown in an analyzer window, or exposed on TCP port
# $uart_port when $uart_port is set (used by the simulation tests).

using sysbus

$build?=@build/fw
$factory?=$build/app/app_v1_a.signed.bin
$platform?=@renode/stm32f407_sota.repl

mach create "sota"
machine LoadPlatformDescription $platform

# Match the 16 MHz HSI the firmware runs on, so SysTick and the cycle counter
# tell roughly the same story as on hardware.
cpu PerformanceInMips 16
nvic Frequency 16000000

# A fresh chip: flash erased to 0xFF, then bootloader and factory image.
sysbus LoadBinary $build/flash_erased.bin 0x08000000
sysbus LoadELF $build/boot/sota_boot.elf
sysbus LoadBinary $factory 0x08020000
